2.0

Changed (architectural — no core patches required):
* Replaced core patching with kea_sync configure hook. The plugin now
  post-processes kea-dhcp4.conf and kea-dhcp6.conf after core generates
  them, using the standard plugins_configure() mechanism. No OPNsense
  core files are modified.
* Survives OPNsense upgrades without reinstallation.
* Removed all patch files (26.1.patch, 26.7.patch) and generate-patch.sh.
* Simplified install/deinstall scripts — no patch application or reversal.

Fixed:
* Boot fatal on OPNsense 26.1.3 caused by removed mwexec() function.
  Plugin no longer calls any core helpers during boot or hook registration.
* Deinstall hang caused by patch prompting for input.
* All hook callbacks wrapped in try/catch to prevent system crashes.

